	\caption{Rewrite rules of ZX diagrams. }
	\label{fig:zx_rewrites}
\end{figure}

There are, moreover, two meta rules
\begin{enumerate}
	\item As all of the ZX generators are symmetric tensors, \emph{only connection matter} (lemma \ref{lem:only-connectivity-matters}) applies.
	\item Since a $z$ spider represent the same linear transformation as a $x$-spider but in different basis, there exists a dual rewrite rules for each rule, where $z$ and $x$ spiders are swapped. 
\end{enumerate}
\end{definition}\label{def:zx_rewrites}

The suprising property of ZX rewrite rules is that they are \emph{complete} in the following sense. 

\begin{theorem}[Completeness of ZX rewrite rules]
	For any two ZX diagrams $D_1$ and $D_2$, if they represent the same tensor, then there exists a sequence of rewrites from definition \ref{def:zx_rewrites} that transforms $D_1$ into $D_2$.
\end{theorem}

