\begin{definition}[Graph-like ZX diagrams]
	A ZX diagram is called \define{graph-like} if it satisfies the following conditions:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item All spiders are $z$-spiders.
		\item All edges are Hadamard edges (dashed-blue edges).
		\item There are no parallel edges or self-loops.
		\item Every input and output is connected to a spider, and every spider is connected to at most one input or output.
	\end{enumerate}
\end{definition}


